body: "Propose a pull request on endojs/endo-but-for-bots, base llm, that makes the private workspaces behind @endo/exo-git and @endo/agentry publishable, on one condition: they may only ever be published as dev-* prereleases (to npm.minion.town), never to latest and never by the master release path.\n\nWhy: the garden publishes llm's public packages to npm.minion.town as dev-* releases (garden devpublish). Three public packages cannot go today, because each depends at run time on a private workspace that npm cannot resolve: @endo/exo-git on @endo/pubsub, @endo/agentry on @endo/daemon, and @endo/agent-tools on @endo/exo-git. The maintainer asked for this change.\n\nThe workspaces to open, at llm 0368767 (the full closure; check it again at the current tip):\n- @endo/pubsub 0.1.0\n- @endo/daemon 2.5.3, which needs @endo/daemon-cas 0.1.0, @endo/git 0.0.0, @endo/host-spawner 0.0.0, @endo/ocapn-noise 0.1.0 and @endo/relay-server 0.1.0\nWith all seven open, all 74 public workspaces can be published and none is excluded.\n\nHistory to respect: @endo/daemon (with @endo/cli) was made private upstream in 986af720a (Erik Marks, 2024-02-15), \"to prevent accidentally publishing @endo/daemon and @endo/cli\". This change reverses that on llm only. The pull request description must say so and show how the dev-only condition keeps that intent. Do not open @endo/cli.\n\nThe condition must be enforced by the repository, not by convention. Choose the mechanism and justify it; for example:\n- mark each opened package dev-only in its package.json (for instance publishConfig.registry set to https://npm.minion.town, whose policy refuses anything but dev-* prereleases), and verify npm's actual precedence between publishConfig and a --registry flag before relying on it;\n- make scripts/release-npm.mjs refuse to publish a dev-only package unless its version is a -dev. prerelease and its tag starts with dev-;\n- keep Changesets from versioning or tagging them as releases on master, if needed.\nAdd tests for the guard, so that an attempt to publish a dev-only package as latest or as a plain version fails.\n\nnpm.minion.town's rules, which a dev release must meet: version <x.y.z>-dev.<YYYYMMDDHHMMSS>.g<sha>, tag dev-YYYY-MM-DD for the commit's date, or dev-latest (packages/npm-registry-server/src/dev-release.js).\n\nAlso check that each opened package packs to a usable tarball (yarn pack:all; its files list, its built artifacts, and @endo/ocapn-noise's wasm if the package needs it at run time), and that each has the fields the repo's package checks want (scripts/check-package-uniformity.mjs, yarn test:package-uniformity). Follow the repo's conventions for a changeset and the commit message.\n\nSteps:\n1. Branch from current llm, named dev-publish-open-private-closure.\n2. Make the change and its tests; run the affected tests, the package-uniformity test, lint for the touched packages, and yarn pack:all.\n3. Commit on the branch. Write the pull request title and description in outbox/report.md (conventional-commit title; the description says what, why, the 2024 history and the condition's mechanism, and how it was verified), with what you ran and its results.\nYou have no remote: the steward pushes the branch and opens the pull request."
