report: "---\nauthor: \"builder\"\ncreated: \"2026-11-23\"\nupdated: \"2026-11-23\"\n---\n\n# Report: endo-dev-publish-open-closure\n\nThe job is done.\nIn `worktrees/endojs/endo-but-for-bots`, branch `dev-publish-open-private-closure`\n(from llm `036876777`) holds two commits:\n\n- `60d62a019 feat(release): skip or refuse dev-only packages outside dev releases`\n- `6e189be47 feat: open the private closure behind exo-git and agentry, dev-only`\n\nThe steward should push the branch and open a draft pull request against `llm`\nwith the title and body below.\n\n## Closure, checked again at the tip\n\nThe tip is still `0368767`.\nThe closure the job gave still holds: `@endo/pubsub`, `@endo/daemon`, `@endo/daemon-cas`,\n`@endo/git`, `@endo/host-spawner`, `@endo/ocapn-noise`, `@endo/relay-server`.\nWith those seven open, `yarn pack:all` writes 74 tarballs, so every public workspace packs.\n\n## What I ran and what it said\n\nAll runs were in the checkout after `corepack yarn install`.\n\n| Command | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| `yarn test:dev-only-publish` (new) | 7 tests passed |\n| same, with the guard bypassed (`isDevOnly` check forced true) | 3 tests failed |\n| same, with the package changes stashed | 1 test failed (the repository-state test) |\n| `yarn test:package-uniformity` | 18 tests passed |\n| `node scripts/check-package-uniformity.mjs` | exit 0, no findings |\n| `yarn eslint` on the three touched scripts | exit 0 |\n| `yarn prettier --check` on the touched files | clean |\n| `yarn lint` in pubsub, git, host-spawner, daemon-cas, ocapn-noise, relay-server, daemon | all exit 0 (warnings only, all from existing code) |\n| `yarn tsc` in pubsub, exo-git, agentry | exit 0 |\n| pubsub tests (`ava --config ../../ava-endo-lockdown.config.mjs`) | 31 passed |\n| `yarn pack:all` (after building `ses`, which CI's `yarn build` does) | 74 tarballs |\n| the guard run over the 74 real tarballs | no tag or `latest`: 67 published, the 7 skipped; `dev-latest` with their plain versions: the 7 refused |\n| `npm publish --dry-run` with `publishConfig.registry` set (npm 10.9.4) | plain: npm.minion.town; `--registry` flag: **the flag wins**; `npm_config_registry`: npm.minion.town |\n| `garden prose diff llm` | no findings |\n\nTarball contents I checked:\n\n- `@endo/ocapn-noise` ships `gen/ocapn-noise.wasm`, which is tracked in git and exported as `./wasm-module`.\n- `@endo/daemon` ships every worker and manager file it loads through `new URL(..., import.meta.url)`, except `bus-worker-node.js`.\n  That file is absent from the source tree too, so it is an existing dangling default, not a packing gap; it is only a fallback when `ENDO_WORKER_SUBPROCESS_PATH` is unset.\n- ts-node-pack checks every file that `main`, `exports` and `bin` name, and passed for all seven.\n\nI did not run the Verdaccio smoke test (`yarn smoketest:publish`), any real publish, or the full workspace test suite.\nI did not run the daemon's tests, because only its package.json changed.\n\n## Open questions for the maintainer\n\n- `@endo/exo-git`, `@endo/agentry` and `@endo/agent-tools` are public and not dev-only.\n  A master release would publish them to npmjs while their new dependencies are skipped, so they would not install from npmjs.\n  That was already true before this change, when those dependencies were private.\n  If they too should only ever be dev releases, the same `publishConfig.registry` marker does it; the job did not ask for it, so I left them alone.\n- Changesets still versions and tags the seven packages on master, as it already did while they were private (`privatePackages.version` and `.tag` are true).\n  I left that alone: no version Changesets produces gets past the guard.\n  Adding them to `ignore` would also stop changesets that name them together with other packages.\n- How garden devpublish calls the release: I assumed it rewrites versions to the dev form and passes `--tag dev-…` to `yarn release:npm`.\n  If it calls `npm publish` directly, `publishConfig.registry` still routes the publish to npm.minion.town, but only if it doesn't pass `--registry`.\n\n## Environment notes (the slot, not the project)\n\n- `garden project add` failed with git's \"dubious ownership\" error until I wrote `safe.directory = *` into the slot's `~/.gitconfig`.\n- Corepack under the slot home fails: the home's `package.json` says `\"type\": \"module\"`, so the cached `yarn.js` loads as ESM.\n  `COREPACK_HOME=/tmp/…` fixes it.\n- `/tmp` is mounted noexec, so every `yarn run` script fails with \"permission denied: <bin>\" until `TMPDIR` points at a directory where files can run.\n  `scripts/pack-all.mjs` also spawns `yarn` by name, so it needs a `yarn` on `PATH`.\n- No git identity is configured, so the commits are authored `builder <builder@garden.invalid>`.\n\n---\n\n## Proposed pull request\n\n**Title:** `feat: publish the private closure behind exo-git and agentry as dev-only prereleases`\n\n**Body:**\n\n### What\n\nOpens seven private workspaces so that `@endo/exo-git`, `@endo/agentry` and `@endo/agent-tools` can be published as dev prereleases to npm.minion.town:\n\n- `@endo/pubsub`\n- `@endo/daemon`, and its private dependencies `@endo/daemon-cas`, `@endo/git`, `@endo/host-spawner`, `@endo/ocapn-noise` and `@endo/relay-server`\n\nEach one drops `\"private\": true` and is marked **dev-only**: its `publishConfig.registry` is `https://npm.minion.town`.\n`@endo/cli` stays private.\n\n### Why\n\nThe garden publishes llm's public packages to npm.minion.town as `dev-*` releases.\nThree cannot go today, because each depends at run time on a private workspace that npm cannot resolve: `@endo/exo-git` on `@endo/pubsub`, `@endo/agentry` on `@endo/daemon`, and `@endo/agent-tools` on `@endo/exo-git`.\nWith these seven open, all 74 public workspaces pack and none is excluded.\n\n### History\n\n`@endo/daemon` (with `@endo/cli`) was made private upstream in 986af720a (Erik Marks, 2024-02-15), \"to prevent accidentally publishing @endo/daemon and @endo/cli\".\nThis change reverses that on llm only.\nIt keeps the intent: the repository, not a convention, keeps the daemon and its closure from ever reaching the public registry or the `latest` tag.\n`@endo/cli` is not opened.\n\n### How the dev-only condition is enforced\n\n1. **Marker and routing.** `publishConfig.registry: \"https://npm.minion.town\"` marks a package dev-only and sends a plain `npm publish` of it to npm.minion.town.\n   npm.minion.town refuses anything but a `<x.y.z>-dev.<YYYYMMDDHHMMSS>.g<sha>` version under a `dev-YYYY-MM-DD` or `dev-latest` tag (`packages/npm-registry-server/src/dev-release.js`).\n2. **The marker alone is not enough.** On npm 10.9.4, `npm publish --dry-run` of a tarball with that `publishConfig` goes to npm.minion.town when the registry comes from `npm_config_registry`, but goes to the flag's registry when it is passed as `--registry`.\n   So the routing can be overridden from the command line.\n3. **The release guard** (`scripts/dev-only-publish.mjs`, called by `scripts/release-npm.mjs`) holds however the registry is chosen.\n   It reads each tarball's own manifest:\n   - in a release whose tag is not `dev-YYYY-MM-DD` or `dev-latest` (including no tag, which npm treats as `latest`), a dev-only package is **skipped**, so the master release path never publishes it and the rest of the release goes out as before;\n   - in a dev release, a dev-only package whose version is not a `-dev.` prerelease of that form **throws**;\n   - every tarball is decided before any is published, so a refused package stops the whole release instead of half of it.\n4. Changesets still versions the seven on master, as it already did while they were private (`privatePackages.version: true`); no version it produces passes the guard.\n\n`scripts/test/dev-only-publish.test.mjs` (`yarn test:dev-only-publish`, added to CI beside the package-uniformity check) checks that publishing a dev-only package with no tag, `latest`, `next` or a malformed dev tag is skipped, that a plain, `-rc`, or malformed `-dev` version fails a dev release, and that a well-formed dev release passes.\nIt also checks that the seven workspaces are dev-only and that `@endo/cli` is still private.\n\n### Packaging fixes\n\n- `@endo/git` and `@endo/host-spawner` gain the skel `files` list.\n- `@endo/pubsub` drops the `types` conditions from its `exports`.\n  They named declarations that only its legacy `prepack` script emitted.\n  ts-node-pack emits declarations only for packages with TypeScript sources, so `pack:all` failed on it.\n  Its tarball now ships the JavaScript modules without declarations.\n- `@endo/ocapn-noise` already ships `gen/ocapn-noise.wasm`, which it needs at run time.\n\n### Verification\n\n- `yarn test:dev-only-publish`: 7 passed; with the guard bypassed, 3 fail; with the package changes reverted, the repository-state test fails.\n- `yarn test:package-uniformity`: 18 passed; `node scripts/check-package-uniformity.mjs`: no findings.\n- `yarn lint` in each of the seven packages: no errors. `tsc` in pubsub, exo-git and agentry: clean. pubsub tests: 31 passed.\n- `yarn pack:all` (after `yarn build` for `ses`): 74 tarballs.\n- The guard run over those 74 tarballs: with no tag or `latest`, 67 publish and exactly the seven are skipped; with `dev-latest` and their current plain versions, all seven are refused.\n- Not run: `yarn smoketest:publish`, a real publish.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n"
